From c9c13dd50dd5afc0a705313ba3c629d5fab9bb0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anmoti <77442643+anmoti@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:50:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] xwayland: support zero scaling

Add wlr_xwayland_set_scale(): X11 clients render at `scale` times the
compositor's logical coordinates and Xwayland's surfaces are shown
downscaled, like Xwayland on an unscaled output (Hyprland's
force_zero_scaling). This keeps X11 clients sharp at fractional scales.

wlr_surface gains client_scale, applied to the surface size and the
opaque/input regions; the seat converts pointer/touch coordinates and
cursor hotspots, and the xwm converts X11 geometry, size hints and
workareas.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012X41FaHDG1j8zRZcCfwo6r
